findings:
GRAMMAR SHAPE — MERGE FORMATS 2 AND 3 INTO ONE INLINE ALTERNATIVE. Today performStatement (CobolControlFlow.g4:18) has two separate inline alts (:26 `PERFORM performOptions+ statementBlock* END_PERFORM`, :27 `PERFORM statementBlock+ END_PERFORM`). Adding a third inline alt for Format 3 would force ALL(*) to look ahead across an entire arbitrary-length body to decide WHEN-vs-END-PERFORM. Collapse instead:

    | PERFORM performInlineHead? statementBlock*
        performWhenPhrase* performWhenOther? performWhenCommon? performFinally?
      END_PERFORM

    performInlineHead  : performOptions+ | performLocationPhrase ;
    performLocationPhrase : WITH LOCATION | {is2023()}? LOCATION ;
    performWhenPhrase  : WHEN EXCEPTION useOnTarget statementBlock*
                       | WHEN useEcEntry+ statementBlock* ;
    performWhenOther   : WHEN OTHER  EXCEPTION? statementBlock* ;
    performWhenCommon  : WHEN COMMON EXCEPTION? statementBlock* ;
    performFinally     : FINALLY statementBlock* ;

One inline alternative ⇒ zero cross-format prediction. The illegal combinations it now admits (times/until/varying together with WHEN/FINALLY/LOCATION) are rejected at bind — exactly the established superset-parse posture (cf. unlockStatement / deleteFileStatement / the boolExprAhead 'superset parse — residue migration' comments).
